      "start": 1500,
      "details": "<p class=\"p1\"><em>Der-ta\u2018y\u012bn-i \u1e24ud\u016bd-\u0131 Vil\u0101yet-i Yemen</em> (Determining the Boundaries of the Province of Yemen): Since these lands lie to the right (south) of the territory of <em>Mekke</em> (Mecca), they have been called <em>Yemen</em>. Likewise, <em>\u015e\u0101m</em> (Syria) lies to the north, and thus it has been designated by that name. In its essence, <em>Yemen</em> is a very vast and broad land. It lies opposite the territory of <em>Berber</em> (the Berber lands / North Africa). In ancient times, the distance between <em>Yemen</em> and the sea was great, and a mountain lay between them as a barrier. But one of the kings, wishing to exact vengeance upon some of his enemies, ordered that mountain to be cut open and excavated. As a result, the sea poured forth onto those coasts and caused the destruction of many peoples and nations. [translation]</p>",
